Public specification:
Given the state-assigned table shown below, implement the logic functions Y[0] and z.
// Present state y[2:0] | Next state Y[2:0] x=0, Next state Y[2:0] x=1 | Output z
// 000 | 000, 001 | 0
// 001 | 001, 100 | 0
// 010 | 010, 001 | 0
// 011 | 001, 010 | 1
// 100 | 011, 100 | 1


Input widths {'x': 1, 'y': 3}; output widths {'Y0': 1, 'z': 1}. Clock clk; sample after the posedge edge has settled. Each row's values are driven before the sampled edge. Optional mid input changes occur AFTER sampling, before the other edge, and are carried to the start of the next row. Protocol seed 20261121.
Return only executable Python with function reference(vectors). For each row return a dictionary with every output and a concrete unsigned integer within that output's bit width, even when power-up is unspecified. Preserve timing and process mid changes at the correct point. No imports, classes, prints, external files or executable code outside functions. Comments may label the contract rules.
Veri-Sure contract:
{"module_name":"top_module","io":[{"name":"clk","dir":"input","width":1,"description":"Clock; sample after posedge has settled."},{"name":"x","dir":"input","width":1,"description":"Input selecting next-state branch."},{"name":"y","dir":"input","width":3,"description":"Present state y[2:0]."},{"name":"Y0","dir":"output","width":1,"description":"Bit 0 of next state Y[2:0]."},{"name":"z","dir":"output","width":1,"description":"Moore output z."}],"clocking":{"clock":{"name":"clk","edge":"posedge"},"reset":null},"timing":{"outputs":{"Y0":{"latency_cycles":0},"z":{"latency_cycles":0}}},"functional_summary":{"overview":"Moore FSM. Outputs Y0 (bit 0 of next state Y[2:0]) and z are combinational functions of present state y[2:0] and input x. State transitions occur on posedge clk.","rules":["Y0 = 1 iff (y==3'b000 and x==1) or (y==3'b001 and x==0) or (y==3'b010 and x==1) or (y==3'b011 and x==0); else Y0 = 0.","z = 1 iff y==3'b011 or y==3'b100; else z = 0.","Next-state table: y=000 -> x=0:000, x=1:001; y=001 -> x=0:001, x=1:100; y=010 -> x=0:010, x=1:001; y=011 -> x=0:001, x=1:010; y=100 -> x=0:011, x=1:100.","Outputs are combinational (latency 0) and reflect the present state and current x before the sampled clock edge."]}}
